``` Detection: Kerberoasting (MITRE ATT&CK T1558.003)
    Data: Windows Security Event 4769 (Kerberos service ticket requested), forwarded from DC01.
    Logic: a service ticket issued with RC4 (Ticket_Encryption_Type 0x17) for a *user* service
    account (an account with an SPN - Service_Name is not a machine $ and not krbtgt). Modern AD
    issues AES (0x12), so an RC4 service ticket is the classic Kerberoasting tell: roasting tools
    request the weak cipher so the extracted hash can be cracked offline. The requesting account and
    its source are grouped so one analyst view shows who roasted what. A fan-out across many SPNs
    from one requestor (dc(Service_Name)) raises confidence further. ```
index=winlogs source="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4769
    Ticket_Encryption_Type=0x17
    Service_Name!="*$"
    Service_Name!="krbtgt"
    Account_Name!="*$"
| eval requestor=mvindex(split(Account_Name,"@"),0)
| stats count as rc4_ticket_requests
        dc(Service_Name) as distinct_spns
        values(Service_Name) as service_accounts
        min(_time) as first_seen max(_time) as last_seen
        by requestor, Client_Address
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - rc4_ticket_requests
